QNX: use the BSD routing-socket and interface code

QNX 8's network stack (io-sock) is FreeBSD's: the default route comes
from the PF_ROUTE sysctl with FreeBSD's address alignment, and link-layer
addresses are AF_LINK with <net/if_dl.h> and <net/if_media.h> -- there is
no <netpacket/packet.h>. Take the FreeBSD branches on QNX.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/src/common/impl/netif_bsd.c
+++ b/src/common/impl/netif_bsd.c
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
 #elif __OpenBSD__
     // https://github.com/openbsd/src/blob/ca647cfa4ec3ccb8360714bc0ebc32a394f7fb6a/regress/sys/netinet/bindconnect/bindconnect.c#L250
     #define ROUNDUP(a) ROUNDUP2((a), sizeof(long))
+#elif __QNX__
+    // QNX 8's io-sock is FreeBSD's network stack: its routing socket aligns
+    // addresses the same way.
+    #define ROUNDUP(a) ROUNDUP2((a), sizeof(long))
 #else
     #error unknown platform
 #endif
